---
permalink: /news/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- The News page was retired on 21 Oct 2026: news became notices. Old links (newsletters,
    bookmarks) are sent on, keeping the item where there is one:
      #roads      -> /living-here/roads/
      #notice-... -> /notices/#notice-...
      #news-...   -> /notices/
      anything else, or no JavaScript -> /notices/
    Excluded from the sitemap (collections) and noindex. -#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}/notices/">
  <script>
  (function () {
    var h = location.hash || '';
    var to = '{{ "/notices/" | url }}';
    if (h === '#roads') to = '{{ "/living-here/roads/" | url }}';
    else if (/^#notice-[A-Za-z0-9-]+$/.test(h)) to += h;
    location.replace(to);
  })();
  </script>
  <noscript><meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ '/notices/' | url }}"></noscript>
  <title>Moved — The Lenches</title>
</head>
<body>
  <p>News is now on the <a href="{{ '/notices/' | url }}">News</a> page. Road closures and roadworks are on the <a href="{{ '/living-here/roads/' | url }}">Roads</a> page.</p>
</body>
</html>
